# Fleet deploy-key registry: public keys a machine accepts for exactly ONE
# command and nothing else. The sibling `fleet-keys` grants a session; a line
# here grants a forced command with no PTY, no port or agent forwarding and
# no X11 (modules/nixos/vps.nix renders each row with those options into the
# same root-owned /etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/<user> file). Public material
# only; the private half belongs to whatever automation holds it -- for the
# manifold deploy row, a GitHub Actions repository-level credential on
# atyrode/manifold -- so a workflow can trigger that one script on the host
# and cannot open a shell.
#
# A key reaches a machine only through a reviewed commit here and a redeploy;
# a line removed cannot connect. Rotate by replacing the KEY field and the
# secret on the automation side in the same hour.
#
# One line per key, whitespace-separated, four fields:
#
#   NAME  HOST  KEYTYPE  BASE64-KEY  COMMAND
#
# NAME     stable identifier, written as the comment of the rendered line.
# HOST     the fleet host id that accepts it; other hosts ignore the row.
# COMMAND  absolute path of the forced command on that host. The caller's
#          command text arrives as SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND; the script decides.

